    49	`docs/revision/posthoc/churn_block.py` gains a `--rates` option (default 0.01,0.05), tested first; with `--rates
    50	0.02,0.03` it reads the new records and writes `churn_mid.json` with the same statistics, pairing and bootstrap (the same
    51	fixed seed), and the scoring of expectations 5 to 8. A combined table lists the five conditions p = 0, 0.01, 0.02, 0.03,
    52	0.05 for both search versions. The analysis code is committed before any run on the new records.
    53	
    54	## 4. Cost
    55	
    56	The first arm cost 4.99 USD (8.87 billed hours at 0.56 USD/h) for p = 0.01 and 0.05, whose measured slowdowns sum to
    57	2.463. Interpolating the slowdown linearly in p (1.182 at 0.02, 1.232 at 0.03; sum 2.414) gives about 8.7 billed hours,
    58	**about 4.9 USD**. Stop cap 8 USD, as in draft 6; watchdog bound 1.3 x 8 = 10.40 USD; reservation
    59	`python3 docs/revision/followup/budget_followup.py --reserve churn-mid-pod 8.32` (grant 10.40). Ledger: 57.51 USD spent
    60	of the 123 USD limit; follow-up category 6.64 of 72 USD.
    61	
    62	## 5. Steps
    63	
    64	1. Internal review of this amendment and the launcher change to consensus; commit.
    65	2. Reserve; dry-run guard; one pod: the gate, then the 36 cells; delete and verify; record the spend after the author's
    66	   billing check.
    67	3. Analysis (code first), paper text after review.
